  <section|Findings in priority order><label|findings-in-priority-order>

  <subsection|1. Actual nonlinear path and one-loop construction is a
  substantive open interface><label|1-actual-nonlinear-path-and-one-loop-construction-is-a-substantive-open-interface>

  The matrix horizon now has detailed proofs: free-kernel components and
  atlas estimates; positive analytic roots; the curvature lift/amendment;
  exact transport identities; and the signed quadratic symmetry. Those remove
  the corresponding old matrix inputs in <verbatim|rg-horizon-geometry.tex>
  and <verbatim|rg-construction.tex>. They do <strong|not> construct the
  nonlinear path history. The latter is not merely another formulation of
  attachment.

  The exact contract is <verbatim|YM.Precision.Kin.Planned>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/PCalc/Loop.lean>. In addition to attachment, it demands:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>actual <verbatim|PathData.Bounds> for every cutoff and rung, with
    weighted row, quadratic-loop, cubic and quartic sums; invariant terms;
    summable zero/first loop moments and their cancellations
    (<verbatim|Lean/YM/RG/PathActions.lean>);

    <item>the top Wilson action's jets through order four and zero top loop
    coefficients;

    <item>a positive constrained Hessian bound, and an actual analytic
    stationary branch with the prescribed linear tangent
    (<verbatim|PriceGap>, <verbatim|Critical>, <verbatim|Guessed>);

    <item>equality of the classical action jets through order four on that
    branch (<verbatim|YM.Precision.ClassicalMatch>,
    <verbatim|PCalc/Chart.lean>);

    <item>the kinetic increment bound <verbatim|\|alpha + G.slopeConstant *
    log L\| + 1 \<less\>= drift>;

    <item>analytic thermal/renormalized actions and an exponentially small,
    volume-normalized comparison of their second derivatives on <strong|every
    two real plane waves>, not only opposite momenta
    (<verbatim|YM.Precision.FiniteBound>, <verbatim|PCalc/Loop.lean>).
  </itemize-minus>

  <verbatim|YM.Stationary.FullPaths>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Level/Recurse.lean>,
  strengthens this by the exact root-row identification and all-period/forest
  comparisons. <verbatim|YM.Stationary.plowed> is the finite backward
  recursion. Its substantive one-step producer is
  <verbatim|YM.Stationary.energized>; its initial producer is
  <verbatim|YM.Stationary.budding>. <verbatim|YM.Stationary.under_contract>
  collects thresholds but still requires <verbatim|Fluent G>.

  <verbatim|YM.Stationary.geared>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/FullPlanned.lean>,
  supplies FullPaths by passing <verbatim|YM.Stationary.pouring> to
  under_contract. The latter is the actual missing analytic cluster, not a
  receipt forwarding trick: it combines the Wilson jet picture and stationary
  perturbation picture, proves a finite-volume determinant comparison, and
  obtains the logarithmic coupling increment from the annulus/momentum
  calculation. Its immediate calls are <verbatim|vintageWilson>,
  <verbatim|saunter>, <verbatim|astronomy>, <verbatim|HouseWord.done>,
  <verbatim|profit>, and <verbatim|absoluteGeode>. The exact annulus
  interface <verbatim|YM.Stationary.HorizCalc> in
  <verbatim|Level/Transition.lean> asks for a common picture approximating
  each finite torus PoleTest with volume-scaled error tending to zero, plus
  <verbatim|\|alphaPay + slopeConstant log L\| \<less\>= D> with D chosen
  before L.

  No inspected integrated chapter proves that contract.
  <verbatim|local-mean.tex> explicitly proves only a linear stationary-row
  cancellation. <verbatim|predictor-branch.tex> constructs the local blocked
  group predictor, not the stationary branch of the full path action.
  Gaussian determinant identities and local packet comparisons do not by
  themselves give this all-torus annulus coefficient and nonlinear path
  recursion.

  <strong|Next bounded work:> inspect/translate the actual
  <verbatim|FullPlanned.pouring> producer cluster, beginning with its
  displayed HorizCalc statement and its two picture producers. Keep the
  recursion/schedule handoff separate, and reuse the already proved matrix
  floor/symmetry. This is likely the highest-impact genuine analytic gap:
  many packet, OPE and centered arguments retain these same funded path data.

  The public binding is explicit in <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.ThroughLaunch.Torrent>
  and <verbatim|.PaidView.ship>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Seaside.lean>:
  retain the original rack and amended horizon, produce FullPaths on that
  horizon, then apply <verbatim|.brines>/<verbatim|Change.engine> to the
  revised path. The overlay preserves alpha and the tower T rows and
  preserves stationary branches away from the top boundary. Thus
  <verbatim|Reports.on_same>/<verbatim|Supplies.heatSame> attachment cannot
  replace this producer; their conclusions forward attachment but not the
  full nonlinear bounds.

  <subsection|2. Finite-menu response: most analytic pieces are present;
  exact same-history assembly remains><label|2-finite-menu-response-most-analytic-pieces-are-present-exact-same-history-assembly-remains>

  The centered chapter's blanket statement that the finite-menu response
  still needs a separate nonlinear estimate is substantially stale after the
  subsequent chapters. The following local pieces now have bounded reviews:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|marked-block-integral.tex>,
    <verbatim|marked-activity-jets.tex>, <verbatim|gaussian-reassembly.tex>,
    <verbatim|forest-average-log.tex>, and <verbatim|forced-exclusion.tex>:
    actual local integral, derivatives, score majorants, ordinary/flagged
    cluster production;

    <item><verbatim|soft-log-fusion.tex>, <verbatim|rg-multisource.tex>:
    exact code/score/marker identities, ordinary and raised activity routes,
    absolute barcode grouping and field pattern;

    <item><verbatim|rg-menu-jets.tex>: actual empty/singleton interpolation
    and the fee-weighted door derivative;

    <item><verbatim|nonlinear-payment-selection.tex>: ordinary Arrives and
    raised Pungent rate arithmetic, two forced payments, reset requests and
    one common future delay;

    <item><verbatim|rg-price-receipts.tex>: shipment, probe, purchase,
    lodging and credit tariff inequalities;

    <item>the Volant subsection of <verbatim|rg-construction.tex>: paid terms
    to per-box polynomial response, including marked origin/occupancy price;

    <item><verbatim|local-transfer.tex> and
    <verbatim|centered-construction.tex>: the resulting Duty transfer and
    downward Served induction.
  </itemize-minus>

  The short source join is <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.Many.ripe>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Tanger.lean>, followed by
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.paneer>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Wax.lean>. Direct reads show exactly what
  remains to identify:

  <\enumerate>
    <item>Fix the <strong|same> Spring, input representation, output
    <verbatim|H.result x>, door <verbatim|sandboxK H x>, selected menu, and
    allowance. Arrives extracts its Captain/Herd/Bikes witnesses on this
    Spring. HasSlots supplies the arsenal/local support realization.

    <item><verbatim|Photo.bidding> turns the offer into the Plot.
    <verbatim|Many.usable> and <verbatim|Many.crowd2> are the two distinct
    paid rows; the raised row uses Pungent, not the ordinary receipt with its
    smaller cap. <verbatim|Photo.shade> uses the actual singleton derivative
    to construct the polynomial output.

    <item>Shrink the logarithmic exponent to the output support exponent plus
    1/2 using the paid earn margin; use the Bikes gain inequality to bound
    the ordinary rooted budget by 1. The flagged output remains at support
    exponent plus 1 and budget <verbatim|2 exp(-mu * fineMonitor^2 / 16)>.
    The offer threshold is the input exponent minus 4.

    <item>In paneer use the exact adjacent relation
    <verbatim|hatBeta(m+1)=betaF(G,hatBeta(m),L)> and the same actual
    input/output identifications. Tariff.probeT/small/buy/lodging/credits
    then give the three Duty inequalities. This is a substitution and binding
    proof, not a new Gaussian estimate.
  </enumerate>

  <strong|Next bounded work:> write this exact join, with crossreferences to
  the existing local proofs and the inherited funded Spring hypothesis. It
  can remove the old finite-menu and separate tariff inputs from the centered
  result <strong|relative to> that funded history. It cannot yet remove the
  FullPaths/PaidView input of item 1. Do not revive the optional
  Cook/Multi/Overlay route; the actual public route is Tanger/Wax.

  <subsection|3. Primary/regular calibration: the local estimates are now
  supplied; the common coupon/history handoff
  remains><label|3-primaryregular-calibration-the-local-estimates-are-now-supplied-the-common-couponhistory-handoff-remains>

  <verbatim|primary-calibration-producer.tex> now proves the small primary
  error for the actual heading, including <verbatim|S_c * receipt * diag(L^g)
  * S_(1/f)> and the engineering <verbatim|diag(L^(d-g))>, the extra
  derivative, cropped/full forecast, finite probes and graded remainder.
  <verbatim|regular-principal-producer.tex> supplies the regular
  vanishing-jet estimate through the short/long/large-support cases. Their
  conditions remain the previously retained path/chart data.

  The actual next join is <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Cub.clocksHere>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Crowding.lean>. It constructs the
  <strong|same> heading for three Coupon families plus its forward/inverse
  norm estimate:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|jewelCard>: the primary coefficient error and graded
    remainder;

    <item><verbatim|basalCard>: the regular zero-leading-coefficient coupon;

    <item><verbatim|heavyK>: the forced coupon, retaining its square-root
    forced-allowance normalization;

    <item><verbatim|Cub.leading> and the triangular price: both heading and
    inverse coefficient bounds.
  </itemize-minus>

  The exact contract is <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Stampede>,
  <verbatim|MergeProof/Wallet.lean>, not just its <verbatim|main> and
  <verbatim|regular> fields. Its forced field and map_norm cannot be silently
  dropped when updating phase-quantitative producer inputs. The density,
  exponential-entry and forced-profile parts of Coupon are distinct
  equalities. Existing local splitting/projection, marked singleton profile,
  and forced payments should supply these, but their exact simultaneous
  application to the selected Spring must be exhibited.

  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.chorus>,
  <verbatim|MergeProof/Escarp.lean>, then takes the actual
  <verbatim|Nest.held> Spring, identifies the input and output
  representations, forms one finite set containing every origin-centered
  logarithmic support and selected forced stock tag, and obtains one
  GaugeDoor with Tune for all admissible grades. The finite-motion
  interpolation and G08 one-step proof already in
  <verbatim|phase-quantitative-producer.tex> can consume it. The next
  recurrence is <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.repriseQ>,
  <verbatim|MergeProof/Renaissance.lean>, and its finite backward use in
  <verbatim|Largo.lean>.

  The delay intersection for primary tests (<verbatim|Cub.motions>,
  <verbatim|.../Cub/Direction.lean>) is routine after the existing estimates:
  finitely many grades at a stage and finitely many permitted adjacent stage
  pairs. <verbatim|Legato.resoling> in <verbatim|MergeProof/Leaping.lean>
  intersects this with regular, arrival, raised and tariff requests, but
  starts from PaidView. Common-scale selection proves how to realize jointly
  compatible requests; it does not prove that PaidView.ship's analytic
  producers exist.

  <strong|Next bounded work:> close clocksHere/chorus with exact forced and
  inverse-map prices; cite the already proved interpolation instead of
  drafting it again. This will make the phase supplier boundary much more
  precise, while leaving the nonlinear path producer explicit.

