  <section|Current closure frontier \V 2026-11-12, after soft-curvature
  review><label|current-closure-frontier--2026-11-12-after-soft-curvature-review>

  This is the current frontier, superseding the older chronological lists
  above. It distinguishes a proof still needed in the article from a formal
  source declaration that already proves it. It is a bounded coverage audit,
  not a claim that every remaining interface has been exhaustively
  enumerated.

  <\enumerate>
    <item><strong|Actual annulus coefficient and pre-blocking logarithmic
    drift.> <verbatim|YM.Stationary.pouring>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/FullPlanned.lean>, must satisfy the
    exact <verbatim|HorizCalc> quantifiers in
    <verbatim|Level/Transition.lean>: one picture recording every auxiliary
    torus PoleTest with volume-scaled error tending to zero, and a drift
    constant chosen before the blocking side. The substantive remaining calls
    are <verbatim|astronomy>, <verbatim|HouseWord.done>, <verbatim|profit>
    and <verbatim|absoluteGeode>, with the common Wilson/stationary pictures.
    Wilson, row-quadratic, uniform stationary chart/action, and now
    soft-curvature chapters supply local prerequisites; they do not establish
    this annular Fourier comparison. This is the highest-impact analytic
    boundary.

    <item><strong|Coherent multicomponent flux output and full continuing
    path budgets.> <verbatim|YM.Stationary.transition_cap> in
    <verbatim|Level/Transition.lean>, then
    <verbatim|energized>/<verbatim|plowed> in the Level recursion and
    <verbatim|geared> in FullPlanned, must produce the actual row, loop,
    cubic and quartic output with its weighted budgets, all-period classical
    match, and finite-volume two-plane-wave thermal comparison. The
    path-attachment chapter proves the invoice, factor-64 schedule,
    closed-subspace selection, finite recursion and row-limit uniqueness,
    while explicitly retaining this multicomponent producer. The recently
    proved curvature response, small-field comparison and stationary exterior
    estimate remove several old local inputs, but do not replace the exact
    output construction or its all-period matching. In particular a
    stationary local mean or a positive root is not a full PathData producer.

    <item><strong|One funded nonlinear transition and its continuing
    history.> The local analytic branches formerly hidden inside
    Roof.Sheltered/WorksIn have now largely been expanded: singleton
    inheritance (Brim), graded/marked cluster prices (Height/March/Armada),
    compensated parameter comparison and Yearling continuity,
    healthy-boundary jets and numerical payments. The remaining obligation is
    to instantiate their exact common data and output identities in the
    selected paid construction, retaining Renewed, down.Bounds, admissible
    initial action, width/preExponent conditions, dictionaries and
    access/Port/Intake/Stamp/Cash clauses. <verbatim|ThroughLaunch.sailsW>
    (FullVolume/Roll/Fiscal.lean), not the weaker Seaside.sailsV alone, is
    the relevant amplified public route. Do not count arbitrary independently
    selected local receipts as this simultaneous package.

    <item><strong|Selected history to the full mesh and phase approximants.>
    The background-path, coupled-background, marked-kernel, local-source and
    fixed-rung chapters prove the analytic convergence implications. The
    selected-history-limits candidate is now being reviewed to bind them to
    Cadre/Amplify/MailBox and the actual activities. Public compatibility is
    verified: <verbatim|FundedCompanySelection.company> preserves companyK's
    Cadre and Amplify on the same Directed/Alloy object, and
    <verbatim|RG05Joint.engageWithCustodyFactor> constructs Locrian literally
    from that pair. Remaining service binding must identify this same run's
    branch confluence/credit, pond/migration/occupancy/Drake data, Served
    transfer and fixed-rung limits. Full-mesh finite differences and
    <verbatim|FullVolume.positioned> then consume the corresponding
    FixedBounds/Purchased receipts. The finite-menu and heading-history
    handoffs are already proved relative to the funded Spring; their old
    generic nonlinear/coupon-input wording is stale, but the common funded
    Spring itself is not supplied by those handoffs.

    <item><strong|Selected OPE service realization.> The raw algebra, local
    projection and its payments, primary/regular estimates, coefficient
    filtration, grid interpolation and phase-uniform OPE estimates have
    bounded proofs. The remaining coverage check is the actual
    <verbatim|Services> realization consumed by <verbatim|OPE.Orbits.produce>
    and <verbatim|OPE.Nesting.uniform> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/R2I/Campaign/Accepted.lean>, on the same selected
    fields and run. Apply the existing same-door heading, representation,
    matching and finite-menu results; do not posit a new raw-price family or
