  stationary units. Its static weighted inverse, selected Cruise bridge,
  actual response arrays/kinetic triple price, classical cubic/quartic
  pictures, inherited loop, relative determinant price, thermal contact
  cancellation and quadratic pole transport now have canonical bounded
  proofs. The independent remaining analytic producer is the finite-family
  annulus face comparison and its correctly normalized common-picture
  recording (limits-author work). The transition still needs the exact
  same-data assembly and choice order, not a new arbitrary family.

  One substantive germ-algebra step is not yet expanded in the article:
  <verbatim|YM.Stationary.coin_tag>, <verbatim|turn_tribute>,
  <verbatim|tribute_wager>, <verbatim|campaign> in Joint/Symmetry.lean. The
  article's stationary-output construction assumes/asserts actual gauge and
  signed-coordinate invariance and tag-independent germs. Predictor tag
  agreement and constant-color/contact Ward arguments do not alone establish
  the moving full determinant's signed covariance. The source transports
  rocket/worn/cannonade and damage by orthogonal congruences, proves bounty
  determinant invariance, carries transformed stationary points back into the
  original tree chart, and uses tested-germ equality for tags. The required
  ingredients already largely exist (branch uniqueness, frame/predictor
  covariance, Haar/determinant normalization); nevertheless their exact
  assembly is a proof still needed. <verbatim|Loops/Curvature.violet> then
  applies the same HeatG quadratic matching and attachment to get order
  three; this latter step is covered by the existing quadratic/Hessian proofs
  once their identities are explicitly bound.

  The remaining elementary transition invoice is also not to be silently
  omitted. Choose inverse width/prices and the output atom constants before
  tau and A; choose the fine picture widths and costs afterwards; then choose
  L so mu times all required widths fits and mu<em|S0, mu>T0 \<less\>= 1,
  mu^2<em|C0>l \<less\>= 1/4. With P(L) the determinant price, set
  Lambda0(L)=2[P(L)+(d+\|slope*log L\|)B]l. For Lambda' \<gtr\>= Lambda/2 the
  displayed inherited-loop term is absorbed. Finally the recording prefactor
  and decay choose beta(L) and gamma. This is a finite scalar handoff, not
  another analytic estimate.

