  missing bridge><label|refinement-of-package-a-canonical-estimates-versus-the-actual-missing-bridge>

  Bounded reread of the current parent <verbatim|local-covariance.tex>,
  <verbatim|local-mean.tex>, <verbatim|principal-gaussian-comparison.tex>,
  <verbatim|actual-covariance-transport.tex>, and the immediately relevant
  <verbatim|principal-comparison-jets.tex>/<verbatim|sector-gram.tex>,
  against Focusing, Venue/Chips, Subtotal, ChipHeal, Movers, Ideal,
  HeadSwitch and TellerFold. The earlier package A should not be assigned as
  a new general Gaussian comparison proof. Most of its analytic machinery is
  already proved.

  <strong|Already available.> The sector Gram lower/upper bounds and
  local-covariance weighted inverse proof give the uniform positive palette
  and inverse entry bound needed by SameQuote. The exact mean identity
  <verbatim|m-v=E^*v-P^*(Av+ell)> and stationary row cancellation in
  local-mean are precisely the argument of Subtotal.spacing/focused. With
  logarithmic amplitude t=R<em|clearanceFare, its residual has the form
  polynomial(B)<em|t>((1+cut)t+exp(-sigma>cut)); hence upper exponent -1,
  which pays -7/8. The inverse perturbation identity already proved in
  local-covariance pays the finite-window comparison by
  N_window^2*gap_1^(-1)*gap_2^(-1)*entry_error. The row perturbation/Gram
  product bounds in principal-comparison-jets give entry_error of upper
  exponent -1/2, and N_window is polynomial in B, so -1/4 is available
  without new analytic estimates. Gaussian density comparison from
  principal-gaussian-comparison is not needed for StrongScope itself.
  Actual-covariance-transport concerns the subsequent linear atlas/history
  comparison and should not be substituted for the actual sector law.

  <strong|First narrow obligation: actual window localization and
  restricted-coordinate identification.> The existing final mean theorem
  assumes distance \<gtr\>30B from seeds and a common 8B logarithmic ball;
  the principal comparison's physical handoff uses 17B/45B halos. Focusing's
  literal call only gives <verbatim|Clears A x o B>, excluding seeds in
  11B+1, and a logarithmic field on the B ball. Therefore those final
  statements cannot simply be cited verbatim. Reuse their proofs at the
  actual panel sizes: <verbatim|Remote.stockBound> gives
  <verbatim|(B+80)/20>, <verbatim|small_span> gives row span \<less\>=B/50,
  and the tested column is within B/4. Subtotal.accounting/focused show that
  all normal-residual reads lie within B/2, hence within the same B
  comparison ball. At those reads the frozen-coordinate source contribution
  is exactly zero, independently of the arbitrary frozen field and auxiliary
  parameter. The same original global comparison field is used in all rows.
  For covariance, <verbatim|Remote.Translate>, <verbatim|staff_W>, and
  <verbatim|clearance> in ChipHeal give a bijection of that actual principal
  window with the bare window under <verbatim|official>, preserving each
  physical address; outside the window both padded columns are zero. Then the
  existing inverse perturbation argument applies. This is the smallest
  quantitative/locality handoff still needing explicit text, not an
  additional inverse theorem. The bound is only needed at value order for
  this reader endpoint.

  <strong|Second narrow obligation: identify the flat reference with the
  retained conditional curvature covariance.> The principal insertion
  comparison uses a curved derivative-reference matrix, not automatically the
  full tree-slice inverse in Focusing. The exact missing endpoint identity is
  <verbatim|plane * treeInverse * plane^T = tensor(learned_f - psi *
  learned_c * psi^T)>. Its source is <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Current.cutHead>
  in <verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/LOCAL_GAUSSIAN_LAWS/TellerFold.lean>,
  with <verbatim|through>, <verbatim|fires>, <verbatim|crossed>, and
  <verbatim|spins> immediately preceding it. Inputs are the same fine/coarse
  Floor, positive floors, Larger and Towers.Diagonal, not a generic positive
  covariance. The proof uses the tree representative equation modulo
  gradients, curvature annihilation of gradients, and the cross-covariance
  identity; it retains harmonic modes. The flat precision is identified first
  by <verbatim|YM.FreeResolvent.Affine.identifies> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/FREE_RESOLVENT/AffineGap.lean>, from the actual
  Attached path row, full-root Gram identity and Sworn symmetry. Existing
  predictor derivative, flat stack, tree-gap and quadratic symmetry proofs
  supply those component arguments, but the displayed tree-to-conditional
  covariance identity was not found in the inspected canonical chapters.

  The needed quantitative tail after this identification is already an
  instance of existing tools: full versus cut row tail at cutoff
  floor(B/100000), product bound for their Grams, resolvent identity, and
  principal-window error at inner radius floor(B/60) give C exp(-cB) at fixed
  L. This is the value-order content of <verbatim|Assembly.headComparison/freeHead>
  in Ideal/HeadSwitch, not a new all-order theorem. Sandwiching the
  actual/bare covariance error with the same curvature rows costs their
  squared absolute row bound; the combined x^(-1/4) and exponential errors
  pay x^(-1/8). Do not remove the selected path/Attached/Diagonal hypotheses
  in this bridge.

  Recommended efficient scope: one compact actual-window specialization plus
  the exact tree-slice/conditional covariance algebra, citing all the
  canonical analytic estimates above. No new general density, inverse,
  Gaussian moment or free Fourier theorem is justified by this seam.

  <section|Exact public Nest/Climbs/Freight attachment \V bounded same-run
  audit><label|exact-public-nestclimbsfreight-attachment--bounded-same-run-audit>

  Source pin remains <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.
  This audit resolves witness identity, not the quantitative hypotheses of
  every supplier. The symbol Y is overloaded in the sources: the clock
  proof's Y is a Wait, the construction's outer Y is a scalar price sequence,
  and the eventual Bolt is stored as R.T. They must not be identified by
  name.

  <\enumerate>
    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.selectRunWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric_of_prediction>
    in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodRun.lean>
    applies the corresponding <verbatim|allFactorWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric_of_prediction>,
    then <verbatim|engageWithCustodyFactor> to its same factor, campaign and
    actual levels. The clock producer in <verbatim|NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodClock.lean>
    calls <verbatim|plentifulWithPrediction>
    (<verbatim|Integration/RG05Preconstruction/Bardo.lean>), which calls
    <verbatim|richFaresWithPrediction> (<verbatim|Integration/RG05Preconstruction/Fares.lean>).
    All these declarations are in the same RG05Joint namespace. The
    Clock/Bardo layers preserve the universal callback over a later Bolt, its
    Nest, reference schedule, transfers, doors, Makes, Climbs and Freight;
    they do not select an alternative Bolt.

    <item>In Fares, <verbatim|richFaresWithPrediction> purchases the
    portfolio and its oyster/shower prices before the later universal
    callback. Its <verbatim|intro Y hy t ht' F' D1 ... hx0 hd ht> supplies
    exactly one tuple. It defines <verbatim|Family.mk (Issue.trail Y) ... t
    F'>, applies <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.hearthstone>
    (<verbatim|FullVolume/Hearth.lean>) to that Y, hy, hd, ht and Makes, and
    constructs <verbatim|Chateau b Q Y t F' D1>. Hearthstone yields Scrim,
    Fridge and Hearthside on that literal family. Wcmain and the other
    Chateau components are assembled separately in the same callback; they
    are not all outputs of hearthstone alone.

    <item>The Bolt is selected in <verbatim|engageWithCustodyFactor>
    (<verbatim|Integration/RG05Preconstruction/PeriodConstruction.lean>). The
    reference schedule is chosen first, from stage divergence.
    <verbatim|YM.FullVolume.rodB> (<verbatim|FullVolume/Stage/Rods.lean>)
    then returns one T, a <verbatim|Chosen X T>, and the strengthened
    campaign receipts. <verbatim|Chosen.receipts> is Nest for this T. Its
    construction selects a central parameter in the enhanced Arc and retains
    the same replay when forgetting extra requirements; Nest.born/held come
    from that same replay's Competes receipts. No weak rod or independently
    selected Roll witness is substituted.

    <item>On that T, <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.Boutique.taste>
    supplies transition branches; <verbatim|Bandage.ease> extracts their
    doors. <verbatim|Bandage.coming> (<verbatim|FullVolume/Gables/Pillar.lean>)
    returns one transfer function, Makes, Freight and Accounting. Its actual
    producer is <verbatim|Bandage.Branch.composing>
    (<verbatim|FullVolume/Gables/Major.lean>): terminal summit plus
    summon/voice, actual tickets, finite composeT induction, then
    Work.G08.answer. It uses the same branch choices and Nest. Transfers
    above the available cutoff have the default value and no Freight
    obligation. The literal Run.mk stores T, its Chosen receipt, schedule,
    doors, transfers, Makes, <verbatim|Boutique.mountain> climbs and this
    Freight.

    <item>The final callback application is visible in
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.Funded.gallery> and
    <verbatim|Funded.coverage> (<verbatim|R2I/Campaign/Accepted.lean>):
    <verbatim|h.attentive R.T R.tuning.receipts R.t R.accepts R.stories
    R.doors R.makes R.carries R.books>. <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.again>
    (<verbatim|FullVolume/Cross.lean>) likewise applies the retained Ahead to
    these actual fields. The resulting family is definitionally R.family; no
    conjugacy, second run, Bourse grantor or Marco.squad witness is needed.
  </enumerate>

  Canonical reuse: common-scale-selection supplies the actual clock and
  quantifier ordering; common-funded-history supplies the retained factor and
  funded interval machinery; selected-centered-service supplies the
  strengthened central replay and its same-history local service handoff;
  heading-history-handoff and the centered Freight chapter supply the actual
  one-step coupons and finite backward music; terminal-marked-construction
  supplies the terminal summit/marked identity. Common-scale-selection alone
  does not imply Nest or Freight. Cream is not a Scrim field: its invitation
  requires the separately specified same-family terminal/local receipts. The
  exact callback chain above closes the witness-binding question, while these
  local quantitative premises and any remaining uniform portfolio purchases
  retain their own review boundaries.

  Static reader package update: parent actual-reader-tree-covariance
  (f66794f9) now has an independent bounded pass and supplies the exact
  tree-to-conditional covariance identity previously listed as package A's
  second obligation. Parent actual-reader-local-gaussian-prices (1ccde1f9)
  has a bounded conditional pass for cut/window comparison and the curvature
  sandwich. It explicitly assumes the actual small-window mean/column
  estimates; the first obligation remains pending. No new general
  inverse/density proof is required.

  <section|Minimal mixed-compiler primitive join \V corrected alphabet,
  genuine and white inputs><label|minimal-mixed-compiler-primitive-join--corrected-alphabet-genuine-and-white-inputs>

  Bounded read-only audit at the same pinned revision. Fully inspected the
  relevant French, Mezzanine, Gush, Hem, Diamond, Gardener, Shipment,
  Bonfire, Funds and Unlid files; inspected immediate Offers, Regale, Petty,
  Acreage, Hulls, Spreaders and ReturnTrip definitions. Compared the
  canonical restarted-rank-history, allarity-planted-compiler,
  actual-mixed-marked-compiler, Gaussian reassembly, activity-jet assembly,
  forced exclusion and high-degree price units. No new manuscript is assigned
  by this audit.

  <strong|Do not redo the completed part.> The genuine/white distinction,
  real auxiliary correction bound e+4d, 6omega/8omega purchases, finite
  marked-component bijection, full-support product counting, warning
  Cauchy\USchwarz, connected regrouping and the upper/lower mixed bills are
  already canonical. The restarted history proves the masked
  logarithm/additive correction and q_n recurrence. These do not alone
  construct a literal paid compiler for the actual corrected chart.
  Conversely, merely citing Kraft or BodyGrant would leave precisely that
  remaining input untouched.

  <strong|1. Smallest new producer: one actual corrected Plate and its paid
  body alphabet.> The endpoint is <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Soft.accepts_stock>
  in <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Soft/French.lean>.
  It fixes one Draft H and Plate M before any output representation Q; for
  every Q with Q.p=v.bp and 25 radiusB(retime x)+30\<less\>=Q.p.B it gives
  Veins for white(v.source) and BodyGrant for genuine v.source on the same
  shifted sprouting alphabet. It assumes patch Branches, LocalRatio, positive
  footprint reserve t, eventual Granite, eventual Wax.Peaking, positive
  m,K,epsilon,W, d\<gtr\>=0, 2K\<less\>=m/2 and 2*i.era.coast.a\<less\>=K/4.
  Its scope is every x in [s/2,s], Escalates, n\<less\>=stretch, Tissue and
  Seeks(neutral v). Preserve these actual parameter identities; nominal
  Lawful at an unrelated budget is insufficient.

  The central missing specialization is <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Pump.foreshadows>
  in <verbatim|Opacity/Gush.lean>. Its actual Helps fields include same path
  and clip, Alongside beds, actual source beta in [betaF(x)/2,2 betaF(x)],
  source threshold phase(betaF(x)), arc=d<em|fiery(retime x), actual Lawful
  bounds Gamma\<less\>=betaF(retime x)^(1/8), delta\<less\>=retime(x)^(-1/2),
  source/coarse radius comparison, LaneCounts, positive footprint reserve,
  and Hefts on the actual candidate. Together with Certified, the same
  Q.Stock, noises and the two Physical.parcel receipts at indices 0 and 1, it
  constructs base\<less\>=-alpha>hot(betaF(x))^2*shares and a nonnegative
  auxiliary Hit price \<less\>=garlic(retime x). The precise short proof
  still needed in prose is its literal field substitution and bounded
  extension: issued decomposes spoolLift into owner posting plus tenders;
  paltry clamps each owner function between a finite lower bound and its
  negative upper price while agreeing on Playing; Petty.issue_invoice uses
  common motion-averaged local functions and exponentiates their individually
  small amplitudes. Tenders is the exact sum
  penury+tallyQ+froth+nightly+introTax+showTax+lining+Ancestor.terra.
  Existing mean/action, determinant, chart, inherited and warning chapters
  should supply these value bounds after an explicit table of actual
  functions, supports and currency conversions. No additional full all-order
  activity or Gaussian chapter is warranted.

  The scalar total in Gush is l=q+q+y^4 nu+(q+(nu+nu))+q+a, q=y^(-1/8),
  nu=y^(-5), a=y^(-1/24); 2l\<less\>=garlic(y), l\<less\>=1.
  <verbatim|Pump.Ancestor.abound> in Opacity/Regale is the inherited piece:
  it requires the exact footprint reserve, B_coarse\<less\>=walls(y),
  B_fine\<less\>=2B_coarse, beta\<less\>=4y, threshold\<less\>=2fiery(y),
  LaneCounts and those Lawful bounds. Canonical inherited-activity-prices
  supplies its support/length payment mechanism; the missing item is the
  same-data value specialization and exponent bookkeeping, not its general
  convolution proof.

  <strong|2. Retain two analytic inputs until their exact matches are
  checked.> <verbatim|Pump.Granite> and <verbatim|excels> (Opacity/Mezzanine)
  comprise March/Coupler, Annulus1AD.Seen, DeepDoors and Beacons.
  <verbatim|Pump.ballot> turns them into Pupil at
  q=epsilon<em|fiery/coupling(beta). Pupil in Opacity/Acreage is an
  all-Matched palette Pours bound plus the exact local implication Toned(2
  radiusB,q)=\<gtr\>sock=0. This is closely related to the assigned
  guarded-reader/warning work, but its all-Matched domain and exact socket
