  <section|Actual coherent stress normalization and free Ward
  endpoint><label|actual-coherent-stress-normalization-and-free-ward-endpoint>

  Bounded source audit at pin 3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464. Read
  <verbatim|Next/UV_STRESS/{Limit,Dimension,Focus,Local}.lean>,
  <verbatim|UVNext/FREE_STRESS_CERTIFICATE/{Choose,Consumer,Certificate}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Next/MAXWELL/{Lit,Beacon,Taxes}.lean>, and the canonical
  normalization portion of <verbatim|Pert/Lifted.lean>. ShellForce was
  inspected only through its conservation argument; the upstream pulse-flux
  proofs below were located, not audited. No new manuscript or source
  changes.

  <strong|The finite normalization is not another positivity proof.>
  <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.produce_current> uses the same coherent scaling
  X, Approaches and Stable, and the exact reference FreeDiv. For a nonzero
  conserved physical B, pull back the full field <verbatim|r_k^4 B> by the
  grade-four isomorphism; divide its norm by the fixed nonzero reference
  stress norm to define the positive scale. No uniform positive lower bound
  on this scale is asserted. Sphere compactness yields a subsequential limit.
  Signed reality and symmetry are closed; centering follows from one-point
  tested convergence for moving labels, not from an assumption that the
  finite isomorphisms preserve expectations. Divergence passes by convergence
  of the rescaled derivative operators. The one-dimensional real kernel gives
  R=cJ with \|c\|=1; choose the sign of the physical B once. Subsequent
  narrowing reindexes this same curve, preserving Approaches and Stable.
  <verbatim|focused_track> takes finite tails for the finitely many requested
  grades, orders and compact windows. Canonical trace-calibration already
  supplies corrected compatible lifts, centering equivalence and finite rank
  stability; trace-free-rank supplies the low-grade reference kernel.

  <strong|A substantive short convergence join still needs explicit
  coverage.> <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.scaled_identity>,
  <verbatim|head_tilt>, and <verbatim|bend_limit> in Focus prove
  <verbatim|D_{k,a}=r_k U_{k,d+1}^{-1} W.deriv_a U_{k,d} -\<gtr\> V.deriv_a>
  in operator norm. The proof is chain rule plus integration by parts, then a
  finite family of separating tests: their matrices A_k converge to an
  injective A, and A_k D_k v converges to A D_free v, so a finite left
  inverse recovers D_k. The inspected calibration chapter does not itself
  prove this derivative convergence. Focus.flowing/closed_path supplies
  moving-label derivative closure. Local's GradientFamily argument upgrades
  the uniform bounded-test Approaches estimates to compact smooth
  convergence: Fourier modulation retains the same test-amplitude bound;
  repeated integration by parts gives small weighted Fourier bounds; an
  exponent above the configuration dimension gives an integrable majorant;
  Fourier inversion and finite bump covers yield uniform convergence, then
  derivative induction. Ordinary weak convergence and smoothness alone are
  insufficient. This is separate from the lattice author's annular Ward
  construction. Parent owns the normalization draft and has received this
  boundary.

  <strong|FreeDiv is chiefly a canonical application; fire's Ward input is
  not.> <verbatim|YM.UVNext.FreeStress.{rank_on,line_dim,lit_in,law,lit_ne,certificate}>
  in Certificate supplies onto divergence, its one-dimensional real kernel,
  and the explicit nonzero conserved torch. Its finite table algebra matches
  trace-free-rank; all-grade-free-detectors is a separate general positivity
  result. The source certificate expressly does not assert the flux laws.
  <verbatim|Choose.ignite/fire> starts with genuine MaxwellData, preserves
  its hierarchy and derivative/rotation data, rescales and averages its
  stress, obtains conservation from Ward windows, recenters, and compares the
  resulting nonzero stress with the canonical kernel line. It produces a
  common nonzero multiplier, not by itself its numerical value.

  The actual native caller <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.extractible17>
  in RG17/Joint first obtains <verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.maxwell_supplies C hG
  1>, then applies fire, before interacting stations are selected. Thus its
  missing analytic input cannot be manufactured from a later rank conclusion.
  <verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.shines/maxwell_supplies> in Lit uses
  <verbatim|beacon_signal> in Beacon: the literal free translation and
  rotation Ward laws for c times the original stress, with multiplier -c on
  the same scheme/gear. No inspected canonical chapter proves that
  arbitrary-spectator flux identity.

  The minimal free analytic package is the single- and double-pulse flux
  receipts and their Wick assembly. Exact immediate sources are
  <verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.drift_flux> (MAXWELL/Affine.lean),
  <verbatim|angular_flux> (Angular.lean), and <verbatim|two_flux_zero>
  (Repeat.lean), assembled as Taxes.straight_motion/rotational_motion.
  Taxes.fees includes all three double-extraction cases: neither contraction
  at the distinguished point, exactly one, and both. It keeps the factor 1/2
  in the stress expansion and cancels the two ordered contributions using the
  finite double-pull identity. Taxes.moment_force extends to arbitrary Wick
  polynomials by finite monomial expansion, with compact-shell integrability
  proved by petal_cost/petal_green. Beacon then identifies the literal field
  addresses and derivative/rotation insertions. These upstream pulse receipts
