    output: <verbatim|YM.Next.Rank.Tapes.Metering.cost> in
    Next/RANK/Concord.lean is literally <verbatim|Launch C k (F.current k) w
    F.mark>. Franchise returns this Metering on the same event as ShowHours
    and Vents. Soft.Star.rented passes <verbatim|h.cost> to thicket.
    Grows.leaf uses the same Launch.pane in parser, then bush_start and
    cloth; Grows.thicket propagates the resulting same-course Whip.
    Coupons.embroidered uses that same Launch in earn_epoch for the Nylon
    assembly. Corridor is its coup field. These are actual producers/callers,
    not inferred from missing public record fields.
  </enumerate>

  Novena.preFoundK constructs its local S after <verbatim|intro Y hy t ht' F'
  D\<#2081\> ...>: Y is a universally accepted Bolt in the Unlatched
  application. It is not intrinsically a replacement continuation.
  Consequently the remaining binding target is the exact public
  specialization at Y=R.T, t=R.t and F'=R.stories (and corresponding accepted
  arguments), identifying C=R.family and transporting castle's ShapePort,
  shell comparison and path equality, then Paid U C.path.levels and
  B.prices=K into franchise. Its output already supplies the
  Launch/ShowHours/Vents tuple. The task must exhibit these applications and
  identities; absence of a bundled field in constructionRun is not an
  analytic obstruction. Do not recommission generic Alongside, Seeks, Launch,
  survivor or Bush estimates. Parent and lattice author notified; no author
  files edited.

  <section|OPE closure-refresh ledger \V bounded editorial/interface
  review><label|ope-closure-refresh-ledger--bounded-editorialinterface-review>

  Read parent <verbatim|ope-closure-refresh.md>, C05/C06/C12/C13 ownership
  files and the current matching, cutoff, phase-price and filtration
  statement passages. This is a manuscript/interface review only, not renewed
  Lean correspondence or proof closure. The common original Q_n requirement,
  complete-discrepancy character estimate, fixed-cluster/differentiated-list
  quantifiers, simultaneous physical low-degree bounds and auxiliary-only
  further extraction agree with the current chapters. The opening/matching
  reversal is correctly flagged: reference-match uses opening m/matching k;
  OPE uses centered level k (actual opened level K(k)) and matching m. The
  complete replicated-moment +5 price must be retained.

  Requested two ledger precisions: low approximants are indexed by
  1\<less\>=m\<less\>=q, not every m\<less\>=q; and cross-owner
  acknowledgements must explicitly include C16 (ope-history-service), C14
  (finite-rank-kernel-transport and actual equation/insertion relays), and
  C08 (projection-payment-producer). C13 supplies the local comparison and
  selected-history side but does not own all projections/relays. C05 remains
  the consumer/simultaneous-label reconciliation owner; C06 local
  leaf-transfer and C12 actual common-family service inputs are appropriate.
  No new missing analytic theorem or source-absence claim follows from this
  review. Parent notified.

  OPE ledger correction carry: parent refresh SHA
  <verbatim|14ae7f3fdef5a7ccc0851acf0c172943835fdf4c5991a1c711ceeb8d71c20c45>
  now has 1\<less\>=m\<less\>=q, opened K(k), and C08/C14/C16
  acknowledgements. Bounded requested corrections verified.

  <section|Physical Ward final-binding audit \V two source corrections
  requested><label|physical-ward-final-binding-audit--two-source-corrections-requested>

  Read limits <verbatim|physical-ward-final-binding-audit.md> SHA
  <verbatim|7b3dd40ee11093d3e4d834a8a2ac3ca1c60f779022434ebe1fec1bc2712c4c77>.
  Focused source reads: Bid/Angular definitions, Town
  buysBoth/selects/pressured/formed/services/station, Climb/Peaks, RG17/Joint
  actual caller, A06 test_aisle/transverse_zero and A07 transfer/answer,
  Org/Input typed fields. The per-grade finite Watches maximum, common
  grade-test scaling witness, scalar equality across grades via injective
  inclusion, separate services curve c/Q.xi\<rightarrow\>kappa, exact
  canonical reference stress identity, and exclusion of A12 from station
  agree with source. A06 transverse_zero genuinely gives all-index row
  annihilation, while the public A06 interface states the weaker eventual
  property.

  Two corrections are necessary in the audit: MaxwellData.frames is the free
  erasure receipt <verbatim|erases hT.spin T.W>, not ActLaw; the actual
  ActLaw is p.uv.weak (H.weak in Bid.services), passed separately as A to
  A07.transfer. Also the public declaration is
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.extractible17>, not
  <verbatim|YM.RG17.Joint.Run.extractible17>. Author and parent notified.
  This review does not certify all upstream Track/observer or native-run
  producers and does not infer a universal scale witness. No new mathematical
  derivation or author-file edits.

  Ward final-binding audit corrections verified at
  <verbatim|8c1c6532eb36dc91c110b57440934af3367273aa0e40efea3a3440d9bf922dd8>:
  free erasure is now the sibling field M.frames with type erases M.hT.spin
  M.T.W; actual ActLaw remains p.uv.weak, and extractible17 has its correct
  namespace. Actual validation outcomes replace the placeholder. Bounded
  source/interface audit pass for the note, with the earlier explicit
  non-global scope. No remaining correction from this review.

  Correction to preceding Ward audit pass: parent caught an additional
  erroneous qualified name in the table that this reviewer missed: AwayTeam
  is the file, not a namespace. Checked AwayTeam.lean namespace
  YM.Maxwell.Free and theorem erasing. Complete parent diff contains only the
  replacement by <verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.erasing> with its file path.
  Corrected audit SHA <verbatim|bbfce9bded2506cc323f257fb05795b554a17d591760433a64e99ab28ceb5109>
  carries the bounded interface verdict. The prior \Pno remaining
  correction\Q statement was premature with respect to this citation; the
  mathematical supplier distinction was unchanged.

  Selected-course update after actual Fares/Run source check: the
  literal-family Binding seam is discharged by
  Run.bought\<rightarrow\>Unlatched\<rightarrow\>Chateau.reception. The raw
  common franchise stage tuple is a different interface. Its local proof
  witness h4 is consumed inside Fares but not exposed by
  richFaresWithPrediction's theorem conclusion. Do not infer raw
  Tender/Metering/ShowHours/Vents on a particular already selected public R
  from that hidden witness. Existing exported rated/warrant/Market outputs
  may suffice for consumers; prefer their direct application if so. Otherwise
  an exact retained-witness/selection interface must be supplied or the raw
  service theorem remains explicitly conditional. This is a witness-binding
  issue, not a new Launch or local analytic estimate.

  Selected-course final narrowed unit passed at TeX82df1c96/evidence5fe0535f:
  exact Run.bought\<rightarrow\>same-family Binding plus generic Paid
  monotonicity only. Raw frequent-stage franchise receipt for an already
  fixed public run remains outside the proved result. Reconcile actual
  exported consumer results before treating that stronger raw interface as
  necessary.

